{
  "dom_id": "step-e13200",
  "name": "Example: Computing the Cardinality of a Power Set",
  "problem": "If $Y = \\{ 1, \\{ 3, 5 \\}, 7, X \\},$ then what is $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(Y)\\right|?$",
  "worked_solution": "For any set $Y,$ we have $\\left|\\mathcal{P}(Y)\\right| = 2^{\\left| Y \\right|}.$\n\nIn this case, $\\left| Y \\right| = 4,$ so we have\n\n$$\n\\left| \\mathcal{P}(Y) \\right| = 2^{\\left| Y \\right|} = 2^{4} = 16.\n$$\n\nRemember that $\\{ 3,5 \\}$ is a single element in the set $Y.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
